{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791609549,"nonce":"DbegELI/3DWJxbkFEfcYfIVUGc0=","message":"Decision: implicit database creation is allowed only when no old database is detected (a fresh install still works without init); an explicitly configured existing db runs with a note while old data exists, a missing explicit one is refused; schedule is unguarded so timers can be stopped before migrating; data/cache and data/backups are migrated too (the raw cache is load-bearing), other files stay in data.migrated; MOVED.txt goes inside each renamed folder, so a data/jobhunter.db that reappears later is reported as a conflict, not ignored; recursive chmod only inside the data dir or on copies the run made; systemd units pin XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME, XDG_CACHE_HOME resolved at install time and keep WorkingDirectory for .env. Reason: the spec left these open; each choice errs toward never forking or silently ignoring data.","files":null}]}